# KAWAD SWAD ERP 2.0

## Complete System Upgrade, Optimization, and Production Readiness

You are the lead software architect, senior full-stack engineer, database reliability specialist, UI/UX designer, and Google Sheets integration engineer responsible for upgrading the existing Kawad Swad Sales Management ERP.

Your task is to inspect the current application, identify weaknesses, implement improvements, run tests, and prepare a complete production release.

This is an existing business application. Upgrade it rather than rebuilding it unnecessarily.

Do not stop after producing recommendations. Implement the verified improvements in the available codebase.

However, do not make destructive changes to live business data or claim that unavailable external services have been verified.

==================================================
PART 1. BUSINESS OBJECTIVES
===========================

The upgraded ERP must satisfy these requirements:

1. All modules must have a consistent, polished, user-friendly interface.
2. Daily production entry must require minimal typing and few clicks.
3. Attendance must support bulk entry and individual corrections.
4. All authoritative business calculations must be handled by the backend.
5. Google Sheets synchronization must become faster and more reliable.
6. Users must receive confirmation only after successful persistent saves.
7. Sensitive data and actions must be restricted according to role.
8. Owner approval must control final production stock posting.
9. Pending production must remain separate from available stock.
10. Google Sheets structure and Apps Script must be optimized where justified.
11. Existing business records, recipes, prices, and permissions must be preserved.
12. The complete application must be tested before the coordinated release.

The system must favor operational simplicity over excessive options.

Employees should see the controls necessary for their work, not every administrative feature available in the ERP.

