PART 19. FRONTEND SAVE CONFIRMATION
===================================

All business writes must follow this pattern:

1. Validate input.
2. Send the request.
3. Show an in-progress state.
4. Receive the backend result.
5. Verify that the required persistent operation succeeded.
6. Display success only when confirmed.
7. Refresh the relevant view.
8. Preserve user input when a recoverable failure occurs.

If a request times out after the server may have saved the record:

* Do not blindly submit a new transaction.
* Check the operation status or retry using the same idempotency key.
* Explain the uncertain result to the user until it is resolved.

Do not show fake success notifications.

